.TH GIT-WHOAMI 1
.SH NAME
git-whoami \- show the effective Git identity and its configuration source
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git whoami
.SH DESCRIPTION
Displays the effective
.B user.name
and
.B user.email
for the current Git context as a single line, followed by the configuration
scope and file that supplied them.
.SH OUTPUT
.nf
Example User <user@example.com> (global: ~/.config/git/profiles/personal)
.fi
.PP
If the name and email come from different places, both sources are shown on
the same line.
.PP
Possible scopes are the scopes reported by
.BR "git config --show-scope" ,
such as
.BR system ,
.BR global ,
.BR local ,
.BR worktree ,
and
.BR command .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-config (1),
.BR git-profile (1)
